USE NS re DB kb;

-- ============================================================================
-- 99_tiled_flip_logical_box.surql
-- 2026-09-02 — TILED path (sid bit15 CLEAR: builder loc_8c033b0a + walker
-- loc_8c0344d4) record FLAGS 0x4000/0x8000 for parts whose GFX1 LOGICAL dims
-- (hdr[0]/hdr[1]) are SMALLER than STORAGE (hdr[2]/hdr[3]). Trigger: PL2A cell
-- 668 (0x29C, Hail Storm) recs 0..6 = 0xC000 on sel 2334 [6,6,8,8] and sel 2335
-- [10,2,16,2] rendered 16 px off when the whole storage block was mirrored about
-- the pen. ROM read only, no capture. Apply, then 07_dedup_edges.surql.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:tiled_flip_logical_box_disasm SET kind='disassembly', strength='code',
  ref='_marv_re/build/bank03.asm: builder loc_8c033b0a (8720); storage dims loc_8c033be0 (8846: add 0x02,r4; mov.b @r4+,r8; mov.b @r4+,r9 = GFX1 part [+2],[+3] *8); tile count + index-table select loc_8c033c66 (8921) / loc_8c033ca8 (8962); per-tile descriptor write loc_8c033ce0 / loc_8c033cf0 (9002 / 9012: desc[0]=m, desc[1]=count-1, desc[2]=tbl.A, desc[3]=rows - tbl.B); walker per-record loc_8c03462c (10421, facing test node+0x110 -> loc_8c034708 when nonzero); facing-0 flag branch (0x4000 test pool loc_8c0346fc @10477, 0x8000 test pool loc_8c034704 at loc_8c0346c4 @10499); facing-1 branch loc_8c034708 (10543, 0x4000 test pool loc_8c03480e) + loc_8c034762 (10590, 0x8000 test pool loc_8c034818); per-tile step loc_8c03478e (10616) / sign loc_8c0347bc (10641: ctrl 0x10 -> neg r4 X, ctrl 0x20 -> neg r5 Y) / scale loc_8c0347c8 (10649); submit convergence loc_8c034864 (10739). bank12.asm: submit loc_8C1244B0 UV mirror loc_8c12476c (10188, ctrl 0x10 -> U0,U1 := 1-U) and loc_8c12478a (10205, ctrl 0x20 -> V0,V1 := 1-V); corner builder loc_8C124AB0 (10647), selector decode loc_8c124ae0 (10673: xs = flags&3, ys = (flags>>2)&3). bank13.asm tile index tables: loc_8c13699e (7491, 1 col), loc_8c1369de (7497, 2 cols, byte pairs (A=col,B=row) col-pair-major), loc_8c13795e (7760, 1 row wide). bank14.asm selectors loc_8c14D860 (13599, wide W>H: index = rows) / loc_8c14d8e8 (13635, tall W<=H: index = cols). dasm_PLDAT/Output/PL2A_DAT GFX_DATA_00/01: cell 668 = 10 recs, recs 0..6 flags 0xC000, rec1 sel 2334 hdr [6,6,8,8] pen (56,-67), rec3 sel 2335 hdr [10,2,16,2] pen (40,-83); both parts have non-transparent texels across the FULL storage block (hail chunks).',
  note='Read 2026-09-02. label == PC in marvelous2. All statements below are ROM-derived (CONFIRMED) unless marked INFERRED.';

UPSERT finding:tiled_flip_logical_box SET date='2026-09-02', confidence='high', status='inferred',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  statement='TILED-PATH FLIP LAW (sid bit15 CLEAR). (1) TEXELS EMITTED: the builder loc_8c033b0a sizes and counts tiles from the STORAGE header bytes only (GFX1 part [+2],[+3] at loc_8c033be0; tiles = (Sw*Sh/2)/strideBytes via loc_8C1291DC) and never reads the record flags for geometry (rec+4 is read at loc_8c033ba8 only as (flags&0x3FF)>>4 palette-bank). ALL Sw/m x Sh/m tiles of the FULL storage block are emitted for flagged and unflagged records alike; there is no logical sub-rect clip on this path. Each tile is a 32x32 arena slot sampled U[0,m/32] V[1-m/32,1]; a flag does not change WHICH VRAM texels, it only reverses them: submit loc_8c12476c/loc_8c12478a applies U := 1-U (ctrl 0x10) / V := 1-V (ctrl 0x20) to both corners. (2) AXES: record bit 0x8000 = HORIZONTAL (ctrl 0x10 -> U mirror + neg r4 X step), composes with facing: U mirror is ON when facing XOR bit15 (facing-0 branch sets 0x10 when 0x8000 SET at loc_8c0346c4; facing-1 branch sets 0x10 when 0x8000 CLEAR at loc_8c034762). Record bit 0x4000 = VERTICAL (ctrl 0x20 -> V mirror + neg r5 Y step), NO facing XOR (same test in both branches). Confirms re_kb/72; the Ghidra reading 0x8000->U, 0x4000->V of the Steam walker is the same code. (3) ANCHOR: xs depends on facing ONLY (1 = tile LEFT edge for facing 0 [flags 0x0D/0x25], 3 = tile RIGHT edge for facing 1 [0x0F/0x27]); 0x8000 does NOT move xs. ys depends on 0x4000 ONLY: 3 = tile BOTTOM edge (no 0x4000), 1 = tile TOP edge (0x4000), both facings. (4) THE LOGICAL DIMS ARE READ HERE AND ONLY HERE: the walker reads GFX1 part [+0] (lw) at loc_8c0346c4 / loc_8c034708 (mov.b @r4,r2 -> stack@0x24 := lw*8 - m) and part [+1] (lh) in both 0x4000 branches (mov.l @r15,r3 = r4+1; mov.b @r3,r3 -> stack@0x20 := lh*8). Per tile: xoff = m*desc[2] - stack@0x24, yoff = m*desc[3] - stack@0x20, negated by ctrl 0x10 / 0x20, then screen = (floor(E0),floor(E4)) + (pen + off)*scale. Substituting desc[2]=col, desc[3]=rows-row_from_first_stored: unflipped tile col c spans [Xpen + m*c, +m), flipped (facing 0, 0x8000) spans [Xpen + Lw - m*(c+1), Xpen + Lw - m*c] i.e. the tile grid is REFLECTED ABOUT THE LOGICAL WIDTH Lw = lw*8, not about the storage width; with the U mirror the net is the whole storage block reflected x -> Lw-1-x. Same in Y about Lh = lh*8 with 0x4000. CLOSED FORM (y-down, in the upright orientation in which a flags-0 block has its top-left at (Xpen,Ypen) for facing 0): Lw=lw*8 Lh=lh*8 Sw=sw*8 Sh=sh*8; Xpen = origin_x - dx_cum (facing 0) / origin_x + dx_cum (facing 1); Ypen = origin_y + dy_cum (dy_cum = -sum dy); mirX = facing XOR (flags&0x8000!=0); mirY = (flags&0x4000!=0); LOGICAL BOX = X [Xpen, Xpen+Lw] for facing 0, [Xpen-Lw, Xpen] for facing 1; Y [Ypen, Ypen+Lh] both facings; X0,Y0 = its top-left. Block pixel (x,y) of the upright storage image maps to screen (X0 + (mirX ? Lw-1-x : x), Y0 + (mirY ? Lh-1-y : y)) times scale. Equivalently the storage block top-left = (mirX ? X0+Lw-Sw : X0, mirY ? Y0+Lh-Sh : Y0), texels reversed per mirrored axis. The padding (storage minus logical) hangs OUTSIDE the logical box on the mirrored side: left of X0 when mirX, above Y0 when mirY, right/below otherwise. Reduces to the proven flags-0 law (facing 1: left = Xpen - Sw, columns reversed) and explains the cell-668 symptom: facing 1 + 0xC000 gives mirX = 0 (unmirrored) with left = Xpen - Lw, i.e. Sw-Lw = 16 px (sel 2334) / 48 px (sel 2335) right of the block-mirrored-about-the-pen guess. STORAGE ORDER NOTE: desc[3] = rows - B with B = tile row from the first stored chunk, anchored at the tile BOTTOM => the first stored tile row is the screen-BOTTOM row of an unflipped block (storage is bottom-up in screen terms, matching extract_gfx1_atlas.py 186-191 bottom-left logical window and the Steam-side v-direction measurement). So under 0x4000 the raw stored rows are drawn top-down from Y0+Lh-Sh. PREDICTION (falsifiable, cell 668 rec 1 sel 2334, origin (100,200), facing 1, scale 1): Xpen = 156, Ypen = 133; logical box X [108,156) Y [133,181); mirX = 0, mirY = 1; storage block X [108,172) Y [117,181); screen (108,117) shows raw stored texel (col 0, row 0) = the first texel of the LZSS stream (upright bottom-left corner of the block); the logical 48x48 appears upside-down inside [108,156)x[133,181) with the extra 16 storage columns to the RIGHT (156..171) and the extra 16 stored rows ABOVE (117..132). Rec 3 sel 2335: Xpen = 140, Ypen = 117; block X [60,188) = [Xpen-80, Xpen-80+128), Y [117,133) rows reversed (Sh == Lh).',
  note='INFERRED (not traced here, not needed for Steam whose pages are byte-exact atlases): for m<32 tiles the mirrored U window [1-m/32,1] addresses the other side of the 32x32 arena slot; how the arena copy places sub-32 tiles so that both windows hit the tile is not read. Empirically the Steam pixel proof on 8x8 flagged parts and the re_kb/71 catalog gate show the mirrored tile is the same tile reversed.';

RELATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box->cites->source:tiled_flip_logical_box_disasm SET kind='cites';
RELATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box->about->routine:loc_8c0344d4 SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box->about->routine:loc_8c1244b0 SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box->about->routine:loc_8c124ab0 SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box->about->finding:record_flag_axes_corrected SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box->about->finding:emitter_render_model SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box->about->finding:scale_walker_quad_is_logical_dims SET kind='about';
-- promote only after the code-grade cite edge exists (77_epistemics assert)
UPDATE finding:tiled_flip_logical_box SET status='confirmed';

-- Stale tooling comment that still carries the pre-re_kb/72 axis assignment.
UPSERT finding:rip_gfx2_flip_keys_stale SET date='2026-09-02', confidence='high', status='open',
  statement='tools/rip_gfx2_assembly.py (read_cells comment 154-160 and the _asm.json writer 452-476) still documents flags 0x4000 = X-mirror (XOR facing) and 0x8000 = Y-mirror, and emits JSON keys flip = 0x4000, flipy = 0x8000. Per re_kb/72 and finding:tiled_flip_logical_box the ROM is the reverse: 0x8000 = horizontal (XOR facing), 0x4000 = vertical (no XOR). Any consumer that treats the flip key as the horizontal axis is wrong for 0x4000-only / 0x8000-only records (0xC000 records mask the bug). FIX: rename/flip the keys or re-derive from the raw flags word (rotgate.py already reads hf = flags&0x8000, vf = flags&0x4000 from V3.rawcells, which is correct).';
RELATE finding:rip_gfx2_flip_keys_stale->about->finding:tiled_flip_logical_box SET kind='about';
RELATE finding:rip_gfx2_flip_keys_stale->cites->source:tiled_flip_logical_box_disasm SET kind='cites';
